prompts.gemini_image_to_image_instructions:
THIS FRAME:
{prompt}

The attached image is the PREVIOUS moment. It is your reference for light, materials, and colour — carry those over.

It is NOT a composition to reproduce. The text above says where the camera is now and what has changed. Render that. If the camera travelled or entered somewhere, the reference shows where you WERE — recompose from the new position and let the old framing go. If the camera held still, match the reference's height and direction and let only the world react.

Indoors stays indoors and outdoors stays outdoors unless the text above says the player went in or out. A room keeps its ceiling; do not open a corridor to the sky.

Never return the reference with one detail swapped. Whatever the text describes has actually happened.

Do not clean the image up or make it look more produced than the source.

{art_direction}

{camera_rules}
